WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.079 --> 00:00:04.748
OUT OF CALIFORNIA AS WE FOLLOW

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.682
THAT BREAKING NEWS THERE.

00:00:04.882 --> 00:00:06.083
A LOT OF NEWS HERE IN

00:00:05.816 --> 00:00:06.550
WASHINGTON.

00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:10.387
POLITICAL NEWS.

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:11.822
WE START AT THE WHITE HOUSE,

00:00:10.521 --> 00:00:14.224
WHERE AN INCREASING BLUSTER FROM

00:00:11.955 --> 00:00:16.593
PRESIDENT TRUMP ABOUT A CARAVAN

00:00:14.358 --> 00:00:17.594
OF AROUND 1000-1500 IMMIGRANTS

00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:19.029
FROM CENTRAL AMERICA.

00:00:17.728 --> 00:00:20.197
THE GROUP TRAVELING THROUGH

00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:22.432
MEXICO TOWARD THE U.S. BORDER

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.966
AND THE PRESIDENT SAYS IT MUST

00:00:22.566 --> 00:00:25.035
BE STOPPED.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.136
HE'S CONSIDERING USING THE U.S.

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:28.639
MILITARY, HE SAYS, ALONG THE

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.107
SOUTHERN BORDER, TO DO IT.

00:00:28.772 --> 00:00:33.010
THIS OCCURS AS NEW CONCERNS GROW

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.379
ABOUT U.S. TROOP COMMITMENT IN

00:00:33.143 --> 00:00:36.213
SYRIA AND A POSSIBLE TRADE WAR

00:00:35.512 --> 00:00:37.214
WITH CHINA.

00:00:36.346 --> 00:00:38.415
CHIEF WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT

00:00:37.347 --> 00:00:40.050
JOHN ROBERTS STARTS US OFF

00:00:38.549 --> 00:00:41.785
TONIGHT FROM THE NORTH LAWN ON

00:00:40.184 --> 00:00:42.085
THE POLITICS NEWS.

00:00:41.919 --> 00:00:43.720
JOHN?

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:44.988
&gt;&gt; BRET, GOOD EVENING TO YOU.

00:00:43.854 --> 00:00:46.423
PRESIDENT TRUMP INSIST THAT THE

00:00:45.122 --> 00:00:47.391
BEST WAY TO SECURE OUR SOUTHERN

00:00:46.557 --> 00:00:47.691
BORDER IS WITH A MASSIVE

00:00:47.524 --> 00:00:49.493
WALL.

00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:50.894
IN THE ABSENCE OF A WALL,

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:54.598
PRESIDENT TRUMP TODAY FLOATED

00:00:51.028 --> 00:00:56.400
ANOTHER CONTROVERSIAL IDEA.

00:00:54.731 --> 00:00:57.467
&gt;&gt; OKAY, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

00:00:56.533 --> 00:00:59.236
&gt;&gt; PRESIDENT TRUMP GAVE NO

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.838
DETAILS OR WOULD SAY IF U.S.

00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:02.372
TROOPS WOULD BE INVOLVED.

00:01:00.971 --> 00:01:03.640
THE MEETING WITH BALTIC LEADER

00:01:02.506 --> 00:01:05.509
TODAY, HE REVEALED HE

00:01:03.774 --> 00:01:06.643
WANTS THE U.S. MILITARY GUARDING

00:01:05.642 --> 00:01:08.812
THE SOUTHERN BORDER.

00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:09.613
&gt;&gt; SPEAKING WITH GENERAL MATTIS,

00:01:08.946 --> 00:01:11.415
WILL BE DOING THINGS MILITARY

00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:13.083
ALL, UNTIL WE CAN HAVE A WALL

00:01:11.548 --> 00:01:14.585
AND PROPER SECURITY, WE'LL

00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.252
BE GUARDING OUR BORDER WITH THE

00:01:14.718 --> 00:01:16.620
MILITARY.

00:01:15.385 --> 00:01:18.322
THAT'S A BIG STEP.

00:01:16.753 --> 00:01:18.655
WE REALLY HAVEN'T DONE THAT

00:01:18.455 --> 00:01:20.290
BEFORE.

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:21.992
&gt;&gt; OFFICIALS SAY THE WHITE HOUSE

00:01:20.424 --> 00:01:23.160
COUNSEL'S OFFICE HAS BEEN

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:24.695
LOOKING INTO THE LEGAL ASPECTS

00:01:23.293 --> 00:01:25.162
OF PUTTING THE MILITARY ALONG

00:01:24.828 --> 00:01:27.364
THE BORDER.

00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:28.465
THE NATIONAL GUARD HAS BEEN USED

00:01:27.497 --> 00:01:30.901
SEVERAL TIMES TO ASSIST THE

00:01:28.599 --> 00:01:33.470
BORDER PATROL AND IN THE EARLY

00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:34.838
'90s, A MILITARY JOINT

00:01:33.604 --> 00:01:35.839
TASK FORCE WAS ON THE BORDER TO

00:01:34.972 --> 00:01:36.340
COUNTER NARCOTICS AND

00:01:35.973 --> 00:01:38.008
COUNTERTERRORISM.

00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:40.510
A PLAN HAS YET TO BE FORMULATED,

00:01:38.141 --> 00:01:41.511
JUST THE IDEA DREW A SHARP

00:01:40.644 --> 00:01:44.448
RESPONSE FROM FORMER MEXICO

00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:45.315
PRESIDENT FOR GENT A FOX, WHO

00:01:44.581 --> 00:01:48.185
TWEETED, "DEMILITARIZED

00:01:45.449 --> 00:01:49.419
SOUTHERN BORDER TO PROVOKE MORE

00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:49.987
HATE AND DISTANCE AND FURTHER

00:01:49.553 --> 00:01:52.189
OUR NATIONS.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.024
SOMEONE HAS TO TALK SOME SENSE

00:01:52.322 --> 00:01:55.792
INTO HIM.

00:01:54.157 --> 00:01:57.027
HE'S CAUSING A GREATER

00:01:55.926 --> 00:01:57.761
CONFLICT."

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.230
PRESIDENT TRUMP CLAIMED VICTORY

00:01:57.895 --> 00:02:00.964
TODAY IN HIS PUBLIC PRESSURE

00:02:00.364 --> 00:02:03.901
TWITTER CAMPAIGN TO HAVE MEXICO

00:02:01.098 --> 00:02:05.402
STOP THE CARAVAN OF CENTRAL

00:02:04.034 --> 00:02:06.570
AMERICAN MIGRANTS TRAVELING TO

00:02:05.535 --> 00:02:07.537
THE U.S. BORDER.

00:02:06.703 --> 00:02:10.974
THE PRESIDENT HAD GONE SO FAR AS

00:02:07.671 --> 00:02:11.775
TO THREATEN NAFTA IF MEXICO

00:02:11.108 --> 00:02:14.011
DIDN'T DO SOMETHING.

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:15.812
&gt;&gt; I TOLD MEXICO VERY STRONGLY,

00:02:14.144 --> 00:02:16.680
YOU ARE GOING TO HAVE TO DO

00:02:15.946 --> 00:02:17.814
SOMETHING ABOUT THESE CARAVANS.

00:02:16.813 --> 00:02:20.017
AND THEY HAVE TO DO IT.

00:02:17.948 --> 00:02:20.651
OTHERWISE I'M NOT GOING TO DO

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.419
THE NAFTA DEAL.

00:02:20.784 --> 00:02:23.353
NAFTA HAS BEEN FANTASTIC FOR

00:02:22.552 --> 00:02:26.790
MEXICO, BAD FOR US.

00:02:23.487 --> 00:02:28.625
&gt;&gt; THE GROUP THAT ORGANIZED THE

00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:29.793
CARAVAN, PEOPLE WITHOUT BORDERS,

00:02:28.759 --> 00:02:31.595
CRITICIZED THE PRESIDENT FOR

00:02:29.927 --> 00:02:33.730
DEMONIZING AT AN ANNUAL EVENT

00:02:31.728 --> 00:02:36.233
THEY CLAIM IS A HUMANITARIAN

00:02:33.864 --> 00:02:37.501
MISSION.

00:02:36.366 --> 00:02:38.902
&gt;&gt; Translator: MIGRANTS SHOULD

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:40.370
NOT BE ABANDONED BECAUSE OF SOME

00:02:39.036 --> 00:02:41.972
TWEETS AND POLITICAL HATE.

00:02:40.504 --> 00:02:44.741
IT IS VERY CHARACTERISTIC OF

00:02:42.105 --> 00:02:44.308
DONALD TRUMP TO GOVERN VIA TWEET

00:02:44.308 --> 00:02:45.042
DONALD TRUMP TO GOVERN VIA TWEE

00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.310
TWEET.

00:02:45.175 --> 00:02:47.644
&gt;&gt; WHILE PRESIDENT TRUMP IS

00:02:46.443 --> 00:02:48.612
SEEKING AN EXPANDED ROLE FOR THE

00:02:47.778 --> 00:02:50.247
MILITARY AND DEFENDING THE

00:02:48.745 --> 00:02:52.249
BORDER, HE IS LOOKING AT THE

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.549
SHRINKING THE U.S. PROFILE IN

00:02:52.382 --> 00:02:53.684
SYRIA.

00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:54.785
&gt;&gt; IT'S TIME.

00:02:53.817 --> 00:02:56.987
IT'S TIME.

00:02:54.918 --> 00:02:57.955
WE WERE VERY SUCCESSFUL AGAINST

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.958
ISIS, WE'LL BE SUCCESSFUL

00:02:58.088 --> 00:03:01.725
AGAINST ANYBODY MILITARILY.

00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:03.794
BUT SOMETIMES IT'S TIME TO COME

00:03:01.858 --> 00:03:05.796
BACK HOME.

00:03:03.927 --> 00:03:06.563
AND WE ARE THINKING ABOUT THAT

00:03:05.929 --> 00:03:08.365
VERY SERIOUSLY.

00:03:06.697 --> 00:03:10.033
&gt;&gt; BUT EVEN THE PRESIDENT'S OWN

00:03:08.498 --> 00:03:11.101
ADVISORS SAY THE U.S. NEEDS TO

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.802
STAY IN SYRIA FOR THE

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:14.204
FORESEEABLE FUTURE.

00:03:11.935 --> 00:03:15.405
&gt;&gt; WE ARE IN SYRIA TO FIGHT

00:03:14.338 --> 00:03:17.407
ISIS, THAT IS OUR MISSION.

00:03:15.539 --> 00:03:18.909
OUR MISSION IS NOT OVER.

00:03:17.541 --> 00:03:19.242
WE ARE GOING TO COMPLETE THAT

00:03:19.042 --> 00:03:22.212
MISSION.

00:03:19.376 --> 00:03:23.680
&gt;&gt; EXPERTS WORRY A U.S. PULLOUT

00:03:22.346 --> 00:03:25.015
COULD LEAD TO A RESURGENCE OF

00:03:23.814 --> 00:03:27.217
VICES AND REMOVE A COUNTERWEIGHT

00:03:25.148 --> 00:03:28.518
TO RUSSIAN INFLUENCE IN SYRIA.

00:03:27.351 --> 00:03:30.454
TODAY, PRESIDENT TRUMP WAS ASKED

00:03:28.652 --> 00:03:31.188
ABOUT HIS RELATIONSHIP WITH

00:03:30.587 --> 00:03:32.756
VLADIMIR PUTIN, WHETHER HE SAW

00:03:31.321 --> 00:03:36.193
HIM AS AN ENEMY OR FRIEND.

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:38.228
&gt;&gt; I THINK I COULD HAVE A VERY

00:03:36.326 --> 00:03:39.763
GOOD RELATIONSHIP WITH RUSSIA.

00:03:38.362 --> 00:03:41.131
AND WITH PRESIDENT PUTIN, AND

00:03:39.896 --> 00:03:41.431
DIVIDED, THAT WOULD BE A GREAT

00:03:41.264 --> 00:03:42.799
THING.

00:03:41.565 --> 00:03:44.668
AND THERE'S ALSO A GREAT

00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:46.003
POSSIBILITY THAT WON'T HAPPEN.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.070
WHO KNOWS.

00:03:46.136 --> 00:03:48.605
&gt;&gt; THE PRESIDENT DISMISSED THE

00:03:47.204 --> 00:03:49.006
NOTION HE IS NOT TOUGH ON

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:51.041
RUSSIA.

00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:53.076
POINTING TO HIS RECENT ORDER TO

00:03:51.174 --> 00:03:53.610
EXPEL A 60 RUSSIAN DIPLOMATS IN

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:57.214
THE U.S.

00:03:53.744 --> 00:04:00.384
&gt;&gt; SO THERE ARE MANY THINGS THAT

00:03:57.347 --> 00:04:01.885
I'VE DONE, NOT ONLY THE 60

00:04:00.517 --> 00:04:03.787
DIPLOMATS, GERMANY DID FOUR,

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:04.321
FRANCE DID FOUR.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.992
WE DID 60.

00:04:04.454 --> 00:04:09.593
THERE IS NOBODY BEEN TOUGHER ON

00:04:09.126 --> 00:04:12.062
RUSSIA.

00:04:09.726 --> 00:04:13.230
&gt;&gt; WHETHER U.S. TROOPS SHOULD

00:04:12.195 --> 00:04:14.598
STAY IN SYRIA, PRESIDENT TRUMP

00:04:13.363 --> 00:04:18.035
REVEALED THAT IN HIS MEETINGS

00:04:14.731 --> 00:04:18.935
WITH THE SAUDI CANON, CROWN

00:04:18.168 --> 00:04:20.070
PRINCE, MOHAMMED BIN SALMAN,

00:04:19.069 --> 00:04:21.338
PRESIDENT TRUMP TOLD HIM OF

00:04:20.203 --> 00:04:23.073
SAUDI ARABIA WANTS U.S. TROOPS

00:04:21.471 --> 00:04:24.207
TO STAY IN SYRIA TO STABILIZE

00:04:23.206 --> 00:04:26.810
THE SITUATION, MAYBE THEY SHOULD

00:04:24.341 --> 00:04:27.110
PICK UP THE TAB.

